    "updated_at": "2018-02-20T10:16:09Z",
    "body": "Per https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#prepare-a-script browsers need to do a \"connected\" check, which means Firefox has a bug. (I want to check though if that check is correct or if it needs to be browsing-context connected.)\r\n\r\nAnother concern here is how this slightly post-insert notification interacts with slot changes. Basically, at what point do the shadow tree changes happen relative to notifying external consumers (which can execute script)?",
